WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:10:00.000
Host: Welcome to the two-hour architecture and planning session. This will be a deep technical review and planning workshop. We'll take a short break every 30 minutes and have two extended breakout periods.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:20:00.000
Alice: We'll review system reliability engineering efforts. We've implemented chaos testing in staging which exposed race conditions in the worker pool. We propose throttling and better backpressure mechanisms.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:30:00.000
Bob: CI/CD improvements — we've migrated to a new build system and parallelized jobs which reduced build time by 40%. We still need to stabilize flaky tests and finalize artifact retention policies.

00:30:00.000 --> 00:40:00.000
Carol: Observability — new dashboards and alerts are live. There were some noisy alerts which we've tuned. Next steps: create runbooks for on-call and run a game day exercise next month.

00:40:00.000 --> 00:50:00.000
Dave: Security review — performed an internal audit and found a couple of medium-risk issues. We'll schedule remediation and a follow-up pentest.

00:50:00.000 --> 01:00:00.000
Host: Break — 10 minutes.

01:10:00.000 --> 01:20:00.000
Host: Resume. Now we'll have breakout sessions focused on scalability, cost optimization, and API design.

01:20:00.000 --> 01:40:00.000
Breakout Group 1 (Scalability): Discussion about horizontal scaling strategies, autoscaling policies, and database partitioning. They plan a proof-of-concept to test partitioning strategies.

01:40:00.000 --> 02:00:00.000
Breakout Group 2 (Cost Optimization): Review of cloud spend; suggestions include using reserved instances, rightsizing instances, and reviewing logging retention. Group will produce cost-savings proposals.

02:00:00.000 --> 02:10:00.000
Breakout Group 3 (API Design): Deep dive into API versioning, backward compatibility, and pagination strategies. Propose a migration strategy for deprecated endpoints.

02:10:00.000 --> 02:20:00.000
Group leads share findings and next steps. Action items are logged and owners assigned. Meeting ends with a short retrospective and agreed follow-ups.
